# GBV – Persian Metadata (Göttingen University Library)

A cleaned and structured dataset of **98 Persian-language bibliographic records** from the Göttingen University Library (GBV system), prepared for digital humanities and library research applications.

---

## Repository Structure

├── gbv-persian-metadata-clean.csv	 	# Cleaned dataset (98 records) 
├── scripts/ 
│   └── parse_gbv.py 					# Python script for parsing raw metadata 
└── docs/
     └── project-report-fa.md 			# Full project report (Persian)


## How to Run the Parser

1. Place your raw GBV export as a `.txt` file
2. Update the input/output paths in `scripts/parse_gbv.py`
3. Run:
   ```bash
   python scripts/parse_gbv.py
This will generate a structured CSV file from the raw metadata.


## Dataset Overview

Total records: 98
Language: English, Persian, German
Source: GBV – Göttingen University Library


## Tools Used

Python — parsing and field extraction from raw metadata
OpenRefine — data cleaning, normalization, and reconciliation
Wikidata — entity reconciliation for personal names (32 of 98 matched)


## Known Metadata Challenges

This dataset reflects common issues in legacy library metadata:
- Mixed Persian and Latin scripts within single fields
- Inconsistent transliterations
- Author names embedded in title fields
- Roles recorded only in German (e.g., VerfasserIn, HerausgeberIn)
- Inconsistent date formats and duplicate fields
For a full list, see the project report: gbv-persian-metadata-clean.csv.


## Future Work

- Improve name authority control
- Enhance reconciliation with Wikidata
- Normalize date formats and separate multilingual fields
- Publish as linked open data


## Contributing

Suggestions, corrections, and collaborations are welcome — especially in the areas of metadata standards and Persian digital humanities.


## Context

This project was developed independently using publicly available GBV metadata for learning and experimentation purposes.
